{**
 * c-close - a button that puts away whatever it sits in.
 *
 * All there is to see is a cross, so its name is said to assistive technology
 * outright, in aria-label: "Close" unless the caller has something more exact
 * to say ("Dismiss", "Close the basket"). The cross is c-icon without a label,
 * so it is silent, and there is no × in the markup for a screen reader to read
 * out as "times".
 *
 * What putting away means is the caller's: c-notice hides itself when it is
 * pressed (assets/notice.ts), and whatever else carries one says what it does.
 * c-modal and c-offcanvas say it through the attributes, as the dialog the
 * button commands and the command close.
 *
 * @param array<string, string|null> $attributes anything the caller has to hang
 *     on the button itself, the way c-button takes them.
 *}

{import 'icon.latte'}

{define close, string $label = 'Close', ?string $testId = null, array $attributes = []}
    <button n:attr="$attributes + ['type' => 'button', 'class' => 'c-close', 'aria-label' => $label, 'data-testid' => $testId]">{include icon, name: 'close'}</button>
{/define}
